From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:19:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: a733: Leave the I/O withstand voltage to the
 hardware

The A733 programs its I/O withstand voltage through GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL
with the one-bit-per-bank layout of older SoCs. The A733 register has
two bits per bank, starting with bank PC at bits 5:4, so a bank supply
in the DT writes the wrong bits.

Do not program the withstand voltage on the A733. It stays as the boot
chain set it, in the adaptive mode that follows the bank supply. The
manual two-bit encoding is not documented unambiguously for banks PC,
PE and PK.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL keeps
the value of the boot chain after boot, after an SD read load, after an
SD unbind and bind, and after loading the GMAC.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
index 6c0eed5ce933..3b8d7dda66fc 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@ static const u8 a733_irq_bank_muxes[SUNXI_PINCTRL_MAX_BANKS] =
 static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_pinctrl_data = {
 	.irq_banks = 11,
 	.pf_power_source = true,
-	.io_bias_cfg_variant = BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL,
 };
 
 static int a733_pinctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
